<title>UK: Novorossiisk repairs complete but wind shuts port.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk repairs complete but wind shuts port.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading Russian oil terminal Novorossiisk completed three days of pipeline maintenance on schedule on Saturday but poor weather closed the port on Sunday, shipping inspector Petrak said.</p>
<p>The Black Sea terminal was closed at 0500 local time on Sunday and remained shut on Monday in winds blowing at force 8-9 on the Beaufort scale.</p>
<p>Four crude tankers, two fuel oil and one gas oil were at anchor outside the port on Monday.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
</text>
